            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/ipmi/phosphor-ipmi-host_git.bb",
                    "line": 64,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Are we sure Yocto is going to split the commas in the right spot with this?  I don't know if their regex is smart enough to avoid splitting inside the [] if you have multiple OEM providers."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/ipmi/phosphor-ipmi-host_git.bb",
                    "line": 64,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "It does seem to be smart enough. It likely does variable expansion after the split. But with:\n```\nOBMC_ORG_IPMI_OEM_PROVIDERS = \"none example nvidia\"\n```\n\nI can see in the log.do_configure, I see:\n```\n-Doem-libraries=['none','nvidia','example']\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/ipmi/phosphor-ipmi-host_git.bb",
                    "line": 64,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "Just out of curiosity, I hardcoded the PACKAGECONIG to have the expanded value and that fails, so the splitter is not smart, but the value substitution seems to happen after the split."
                }
            ],
